&Q000452 = An adab to Bau for Išme-Dagan (Išme-Dagan B)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.5.4.02
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.5.4.02&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div sa-gida A

A.1. nin ni₂ guru₃ mah zu an ki nam-nir-ra šu du₇
#tr.en: Lady, imbued with fearsomeness, whose greatness is recognised in heaven and on earth, perfect in nobility!
#lem: nin[lady]; ni[fear]; gur[lift]; mah[great]; zu[know]; an[sky]; ki[place]; namnir[supremacy]; šu[hand]; du[perfect]
#etcsl: line-id=A.1

A.2. ama {d}ba-u₂ gu₂-gal nin-e-[ne] ur-saŋ X X
#tr.en: Mother @wDN{Bau}, foremost among ladies, warrior ……!
#lem: ama[mother]; Bau[1]DN; gugal[foremost]; nin[lady]; ursaŋ[warrior]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=A.2

A.3. diŋir er₉ me mah-a šu du₇ saŋ# il₂ umuš gal LU
#tr.en: Powerful goddess, who perfectly controls the august divine powers, proud one, …… great intelligence!
#lem: diŋir[deity]; ir[mighty]; me[Being]; mah[great]; šu[hand]; du[perfect]; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; umuš[consideration]; gal[big]; X
#etcsl: line-id=A.3

A.4. su₄-un-su₄-na munus zid nin gal-an-zu# šag₄-ta umun₂ ak
#tr.en: ……, true woman, wise lady who has been made knowledgeable from birth!
#lem: X; munus[woman]; zid[right]; nin[lady]; galanzu[wise]; šag[heart]; umun[knowledge]; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=A.4

A.5. dumu an-na mas-su₂ inim pad₃-de₃ niŋ₂-nam šu-ni si
#tr.en: Daughter of @wDN{An}, expert, eloquent, who holds everything in her hand!
#lem: dumu[child]; An[1]DN; massu[leader]; inim[word]; pad[find]; niŋnam[anything]; šu[hand]; si[fill]
#etcsl: line-id=A.5

A.6. nin a-zu gal saŋ gig₂-ga lu₂ til₃-le lu₂ u₃-tud
#tr.en: Lady, great doctor of the black-headed people, who keeps people alive, and brings them to birth.
#lem: nin[lady]; azu[doctor]; gal[big]; saŋ[head]; giggig[black]; lu[person]; til[live (of a single person)]; lu[person]; utud[give birth (to)]
#etcsl: line-id=A.6

A.7. šu-hal-bi šim-mu₂ uŋ₃ lu-a X X X X X
#tr.en: @wDN{Šu-ḫalbi}, incantation priestess of the numerous people, ……!
#lem: Šuhalbi[1]DN; šimmu[priest]; uŋ[people]; lu[abundant]; X; X; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=A.7

A.8. šag₄-la₂ tuku arhuš₂ sud kalam-ma nin niŋ₂-gen₆-[na]
#tr.en: Merciful, compassionate one of the Land, lady of justice!
#lem: šala[pity]; tuku[acquire]; arhuš[compassion]; sud[distant]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; nin[lady]; niŋgina[truth]
#etcsl: line-id=A.8

A.9. {d}en-lil₂ lugal kur-kur-ra-[ke₄]
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil}, the king of all the foreign countries, @wDN{Nunamnir}, the lord who determines the fates,
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; lugal[king]; kur[mountain(s)]
#etcsl: line-id=A.9

A.10. {d}nu-nam-nir en nam tar-re-[de₃]
#tr.en: decreed something of great importance in the shrine @wSN{Nibru}, in @wTN{Dur-an-ki}:
#lem: Nunamnir[1]DN; en[lord]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=A.10

A.11. eš₃ nibru{ki} dur-an-ki-a-ka gal-bi bi₂-in-[dug₄]
#tr.en: he made you exalted in the shining @wTN{E-kur}, …….
#lem: eš[shrine]; Nibru[1]SN; Durankik[1]TN; gal[big]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.11

A.12. e₂-kur za-gin₃-na mi-ni-im-mah-en IGI RA X
#tr.en: You are the strong spread-net of @wDN{Nunamnir}. @fsux{Anguba} priestess, who provides the @wTN{E-kur} with food,
#lem: Ekur[1]TN; zagin[lapis lazuli]; mah[great]; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=A.12

A.13. sa-par₃ kalag-ga {d}nu-nam-nir-ra-[me-en]
#tr.en: you are in charge of the wine. You are @wDN{Enlil's} exalted daughter-in-law,
#lem: sabar[net]; kalag[strong]; Nunamnir[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=A.13

A.14. an-gub-ba e₂-kur-ra-ka šukur₂ šum₂-mu ŋeštin za-a-[kam]
#tr.en: you are the one who stands next to him with the libation water (?).
#lem: anguba[tutelary deity]; Ekur[1]TN; šukur[food allocation]; šum[give]; ŋeštin[vine]; zaʾe[you]
#etcsl: line-id=A.14

A.15. {d}en-lil₂-la₂ e₂-gi₄-a mah-a-ni-me-en a gub-ba-ni-[me]-en#
#tr.en: Because you prostrated yourself humbly with supplications, @wDN{Nunamnir},
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; egia[bride]; mah[great]; a[water]; gub[stand]
#etcsl: line-id=A.15

A.16. su₄-na šita-ba ki la₂-a-zu-uš
#tr.en: the prince of all the foreign countries,
#lem: sun[humble]; šita[prayer]; ki[place]; la[hang]
#etcsl: line-id=A.16

A.17. {d}nu-nam-nir nun kur-kur-ra-ke₄
#tr.en: entrusted to you the exalted office of accountant of heaven and earth,
#lem: Nunamnir[1]DN; nun[prince]; kur[mountain(s)]
#etcsl: line-id=A.17

A.18. nam-saŋ-tun₃ mah an ki šu-zu im-mi-in-kur₉
#tr.en: and exalted you,
#lem: nam.saŋ.DUN₃[office of land recorder]; mah[great]; an[sky]; ki[place]; šu[hand]; kur[enter]
#etcsl: line-id=A.18

A.19. mu-un-il₂-en nam-nin eš₃ numun i za-ra mu-ra-an-šum₂
#tr.en: giving you the rank of lady of the shrine which brought the seeds of mankind forth.
#lem: il[raise]; namnin[ladyship]; eš[shrine]; numun[seed]; e[bring out]; zaʾe[you]; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=A.19

A.20. a-a ugu-zu an diŋir mah-e tug₂ tug₂-ba₁₃ tug₂ mi-ri-in-mu
#tr.en: Your own father, @wDN{An}, the highest god, clothed you in the @fsux{ba} garment.
#lem: aya[father]; ugu[bear]; An[1]DN; diŋir[deity]; mah[great]; tug[textile]; ba[garment]; tug[textile]; mur[dress]
#etcsl: line-id=A.20

A.21. ur-saŋ {d}en-lil₂-la₂ {d}nin-ŋir₂-su# nitalam#-še₃ ma-ra-an-šum₂
#tr.en: He gave you the warrior of @wDN{Enlil}, @wDN{Ninŋirsu}, as your husband. He bestowed on you the @wTN{E-ninnu} and @wSN{Iri-kug},
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; Enlil[1]DN; Ninŋirsuk[1]DN; ŋidlam[(equal ranking) spouse]; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=A.21

A.22. e₂-ninnu iri-kug eš₃ numun i saŋ-e-eš# mu-ri-rig₇
#tr.en: the shrine which brought forth the seeds of mankind. He has set up your lofty throne-dais in @wSN{Lagaš},
#lem: Eninnu[1]TN; Irikug[1]SN; eš[shrine]; numun[seed]; e[bring out]; saŋ[head]; rig[donate]
#etcsl: line-id=A.22

A.23. lagaš{ki} ŋir₂-su{ki} dim# gal kalam-ma-ka
#tr.en: in @wSN{Ŋirsu}, the mooring post of the Land, in @wTN{E-ŋalga-sud}, your beloved residence,
#lem: Lagaš[1]SN; Ŋirsu[1]SN; dim[post]; gal[big]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]
#etcsl: line-id=A.23

A.24. e₂-ŋalga-sud ki-tuš ki aŋ₂-za
#tr.en: in @wTN{Tar-sirsir},
#lem: Eŋalgasud[1]TN; kituš[dwelling place]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]
#etcsl: line-id=A.24

A.25. tar-sir₂-sir₂ e₂ nam-nin-a-ka barag mah-zu mi-ni-ri
#tr.en: the temple of ladyship;
#lem: Etarsirsir[1]TN; e[house]; namnin[ladyship]; barag[sanctum]; mah[great]; ri[impose]
#etcsl: line-id=A.25

A.26. ki-tuš mah-zu-še₃ diŋir ki lagaš{ki}-a im-ši-gam-e-de₃-eš
#tr.en: and now all the gods of the land of @wSN{Lagaš} bow down before your august residence.
#lem: kituš[dwelling place]; mah[great]; diŋir[deity]; ki[place]; Lagaš[1]SN; gurum[bend]
#etcsl: line-id=A.26

A.27. nin zag dib me-ni šu nu-teŋ₃-ŋa₂
#tr.en: Supreme lady, whose divine powers are untouchable, daughter of @wDN{An}, omniscient great lady, young woman, Mother @wDN{Bau},
#lem: nin[lady]; zag[side]; dib[pass]; me[Being]; šu[hand]; teŋ[approach]
#etcsl: line-id=A.27

A.28. dumu an-na nin gal niŋ₂-nam zu
#tr.en: you have looked favourably on the young man of handsome form,
#lem: dumu[child]; An[1]DN; nin[lady]; gal[big]; niŋnam[anything]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=A.28

A.29. šul me-dim₂ sag₉ nun {d}iš-me-{d}da-gan dumu {d}en-lil₂-la₂-ke₄
#tr.en: prince @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}}, the son of @wDN{Enlil};
#lem: šul[youth]; medim[limbs]; sag[goodness]; nun[prince]; Išmedagan[1]RN; dumu[child]; Enlil[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=A.29

A.30. ki-sikil ama {d}ba-u₂ igi zid mu-ši-bar nam dug₃ mu-ni-tar ud til₃-la e₃-a-še₃
#tr.en: you have determined for him a good fate once and for all.
#lem: kisikil[young woman]; ama[mother]; Bau[1]DN; igi[eye]; zid[right]; bar[place outside]; nam[fate]; dug[good]; tar[cut]; ud[sun]; til[live (of a single person)]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=A.30

@div trailer 

A.31. sa-gid₂-da-am₃
#tr.en: @fsux{Sa-gida}.
#lem: sagida[musical notation]
#etcsl: line-id=A.31

@end trailer

@end sa-gida

@div ŋišgiŋal B

B.32. ama {d}ba-u₂ nun {d}iš-me-{d}da-gan dumu {d}en-lil₂-la₂-ra nam-til₃ ud su₃-ra₂ šum₂-mu-dam
#tr.en: It is Mother @wDN{Bau} who is to give prince @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}}, the son of @wDN{Enlil}, a life of numerous days.
#lem: ama[mother]; Bau[1]DN; nun[prince]; Išmedagan[1]RN; dumu[child]; Enlil[1]DN; namtil[life]; ud[sun]; sud[distant]; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=B.32

@div trailer 

B.33. ŋiš-gi₄-ŋal₂ sa-gid₂-da-[bi-im]
#tr.en: @fsux{Ŋišgiŋal} of the @fsux{sa-gida}.
#lem: ŋešgiŋal[musical refrain]; sagida[musical notation]
#etcsl: line-id=B.33

@end trailer

@end ŋišgiŋal

@div sa-ŋara C

C.34. e₂-nam-til₃-la e₂ {d}en-lil₂-la₂-še₃
#tr.en: You introduced prince @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}},
#lem: Enamtilak[1]TN; e[house]; Enlil[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=C.34

C.35. sila₄ babbar udu inim-ŋar sag₉-ga gaba-na im-mi-tab
#tr.en: clasping to his breast a white lamb and a sheep of auspicious omens,
#lem: sila[lamb]; babbar[white]; udu[sheep]; iŋar[oracular utterance]; sag[good]; gaba[breast]; tab[double]
#etcsl: line-id=C.35

C.36. nun {d}iš-me-{d}da-gan za-e im-me-ni-kur₉
#tr.en: into the @wTN{E-namtila}, @wDN{Enlil's} temple,
#lem: nun[prince]; Išmedagan[1]RN; zaʾe[you]; kur[enter]
#etcsl: line-id=C.36

C.37. |KI.LUGAL.GUB| nam-til₃-la-da im-da-e-gub
#tr.en: and made him stand at the royal offering place of life.
#lem: KI.LUGAL.DU[cultic place]; namtil[life]; gub[stand]
#etcsl: line-id=C.37

C.38. kur gal {d}en-lil₂-ra KA ki mu-ne-ŋal₂
#tr.en: Then you saluted the Great Mountain @wDN{Enlil} and told him:
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; gal[big]; Enlil[1]DN; X; ki[place]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=C.38

C.39. a-a %e {d}mu-ul-lil₂ %e u₃-mu-un %s gal kur-kur-ra
#tr.en: @q[Bau,Enlil]{“Father @wDN{Enlil}, great lord of all the foreign countries,
#lem: aya[father]; Mullil[]DN; umun[lord]N; gal[big]; kur[mountain(s)]
#etcsl: line-id=C.39

C.40. {d}iš-me-{d}da-gan-na %e na-aŋ₂ de₃-eb₂-tar %s mu-ni %e de₃-eb₂-pad₃ %s e-ne-er mu-ne-dug₄
#tr.en: determine the fate of @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}}, call him by name!”}
#lem: Išmedagan[1]RN; naŋ[fate]N; tar[cut]; mu[name]; pad[find]; ane[he]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=C.40

C.41. {d}en-lil₂ lugal kur-kur-ra-ke₄ igi nam-til₃-la saŋ-ki zalag-ga-ni mu-un-ši-in-bar
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil}, the king of all the foreign countries, looked encouragingly upon him,
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; lugal[king]; kur[mountain(s)]; igi[eye]; namtil[life]; saŋki[forehead]; zalag[bright]; bar[place outside]
#etcsl: line-id=C.41

C.42. {d}iš-me-{d}da-gan-na nam mu-ni-ib₂-tar-re
#tr.en: beaming radiantly; and determined a fate for @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}}:
#lem: Išmedagan[1]RN; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=C.42

C.43. {ŋiš}gu-za me ur₄-ur₄ aga zid ud su₃-ra₂-a ŋidru uŋ₃ gen₆-ne₂ us₂ 1(AŠ)-a lah₄!-lah₄!-e
#tr.en: @q[Enlil,]{“Prince @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}}, as your fate, you shall be given a throne which concentrates all divine powers,
#lem: guza[chair]; me[Being]; ur[gather]; aga[tiara]; zid[right]; ud[sun]; sud[distant]; ŋidru[scepter]; uŋ[people]; gin[confirm]; us[accompany]; n; lah[plural stem of tum ⟦bring⟧]
#etcsl: line-id=C.43

C.44. nun {d}iš-me-{d}da-gan nam-e-eš he₂-tar
#tr.en: an enduring legitimate crown and a sceptre which maintains the people and keeps them united.
#lem: nun[prince]; Išmedagan[1]RN; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=C.44

C.45. {id₂}idigna {id₂}buranuna-e he₂-ŋal₂ a-eštub{ku₆} hu-mu-ra-ab-tum₃ (1:gun₂-bi ha-ra-gid₂-e:1)
#tr.en: The @wWN{Tigris} and the @wWN{Euphrates} shall bring abundance, carp-filled waters for you,
#lem: Idigna[1 Tigris]; Buranun[1 Euphrates]; heŋal[plenty]; aʾeštub[early flooding]; tum[bring]; gun[load]; gid[long]
#etcsl: line-id=C.45

:45v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) kun X [...]
?#tr.en: @varh[t25402.v1]{their yield shall be long-lasting for you } @vart[t25402.v2,t25402.v1]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} …… }. Their banks shall grow vegetation for you, they shall bring (?) you rejoicing.
?#tr.en: The irrigated orchards shall yield (?) syrup and wine for you. The fertile arable tracts shall grow dappled grain for you;
?#tr.en: grain piles shall be heaped up for you. Cattle-pens shall be built,
?#tr.en: sheepfolds shall be enlarged for you.
?#tr.en: Your name shall be exalted as king;
?#tr.en: you shall be elevated as prince.
?#tr.en: All the foreign countries from below as far as the uplands shall bring tribute for you.
?#tr.en: You shall shine radiantly in the grand main courtyard like sunlight.
?#tr.en: Your food offerings shall never cease in the shining @wTN{E-kur}.”}
?#tr.en: This is how @wDN{Enlil} determined his fate.
?#tr.en: From the @wTN{E-kur} he gave huge strength to the king.
?#tr.en: He has been made lordly;
?#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil's} words made him a man without rival.
?#tr.en: He directed his steps proudly there and entered the august palace, the royal residence.
?#tr.en: As he took his seat on the shining holy throne-dais, the palace …….
#lem: kun[tail]; X; X

C.46. gu₂-gu₂-bi u₂-šim hu-mu-ra-an-mu₂ asila ha-ra-ab-la₂
#lem: gu[neck]; ušim[greenery]; mu[grow]; asilala[joy]; la[hang]
#etcsl: line-id=C.46

